GEN - a small generative model: a ternary neural net (about 100,000
weights of -1, 0 and 1, 31K on disc) trained on NTC BASIC and Z80
assembly, writing on from what it is given, a character at a time.

  GEN [v:]file [n] [noise]   the file's text read in as the start,
                             then n characters (200) written after it
  GEN                        no file: a program's first lines as the start
  noise 0-20 (0)             the model's choice jogged at random, for
                             variety; 0: the same text every time

The model is GEN.MDL on this slot's drive or on A. A key ends it early.
About a second a character on a 4 MHz CPC; the vCPC does it a hundred
times faster. It is a completer that has read only CyborgOS's and NTC's
own sources: it writes the shapes it knows (Dim, For, Print, a class's
calls), not programs that do what you mean. Train your own on a PC with
NTC's tools/gen (corpus.py, train.py) and put the GEN.MDL it writes on
the disc.
